<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ernst Johann von Biron</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1690–1772</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Ernst Johann von Bühren</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ernst Johann von Biron was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/courland">Courland</a> nobleman who became the favourite of Empress <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anna-of-russia">Anna of Russia</a> and, with her backing, Duke of Courland and Semigallia in 1737. He commissioned Rastrelli to build Rundāle and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jelgava">Jelgava</a> palaces. Briefly regent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> after Anna's death in 1740, he was overthrown within weeks and exiled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>, returning to rule Courland from 1763 to 1769.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ernst-johann-von-biron.jpg" alt="Ernst Johann von Biron" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ernst_Johann_von_Biron_111.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
